
Start with the veggies..
2 Jalapeño peppers - chopped fine
1 paseo pepper - chipped medium
1 large onion - chopped medium
1/2 red sweet pepper - chopped medium.
A couple handfuls of chopped green onions.
olive oil in Dutch oven for frying, get all these veggies frying.
Add salt, pepper, chili powder, ground cumin.
The plan is to cook all of these down to the level of grilled onions.

Once all the veggies are cooked down, Scrape a hole on the middle and.. 
Drop in 1 lb ground elk meat.
Add salt, pepper, chili powder, ground cumin, some paprika, a little pig powder, one tiny pinch of ancho chili powder. (These levels of spice will be up to you.) I use a LOT of chili powder, 1/2 that of cumin and unlimited black pepper. Salt to taste. A -little- shake of Cayenne pepper for heat.
Fry all this up 'till the ground elk is nearly done cooking.

Add in 2 large cloves of garlic - crushed. (Should be two garlic press bowls full)

Cook this stirring for a couple minutes to let the garlic meld in and cook a -little-.

Now add in some jared tomato pasta sauce. Maybe 1/4 cup? I just spooned it in 'till I liked how "wet" the chili was.

1 large forkful of sweet pickle relish. (Seriously magical secret ingredient.)

Get all this blended together. Then add a drained 15 oz can of pinto beans. (Home made pink beans would be much better, but none were ready at this time.)
Also at this time add in a couple more handfuls of chopped green onions.

Last adjustment. 
It probably tastes a little "thin" and harsh. At this point I tossed in a handful of sugar. You basically add sugar 'till the flavors balance out. Once balanced, the peppers will taste like sweet fruit chunks.
